{"title":"KGS math club/solution pairing","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Main_Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Main Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Preparations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Preparations</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Claim_(1)_-_The_exceptional_cases\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Claim (1) - The exceptional cases</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Claim_(2)_-_Pairings_for_small_cases\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Claim (2) - Pairings for small cases</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Claim_(3)_-_The_main_inequality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Claim (3) - The main inequality</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Claim_(4)_-_Rewriting_the_main_inequality\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Claim (4) - Rewriting the main inequality</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Claim_(5)_-_Finding_odd_perfect_squares\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Claim (5) - Finding odd perfect squares</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#The_Finish\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The Finish</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Credits\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Credits</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For which natural numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is it possible to take the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/c/f3c5fd3c25a314c7756f53ae265e91cccf885f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, \\dots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />\nand pair them up so that the sum of each pair is a perfect square?\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Main_Statement\">Main Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Main Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For all even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, except for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16d2dd6712bf62c9be7c300f161ecc6f0b4880f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2, 4, 6, 10, 12, 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Preparations\">Preparations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Preparations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Clearly, pairings are not possible for odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>For numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, we say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a <b>partner</b> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df6a591474ffd81edd37d8d9f52f6f476caa531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square.\n</p><p>The main statement is established through the following claims.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Claim_.281.29_-_The_exceptional_cases\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Claim_(1)_-_The_exceptional_cases\">Claim (1) - The exceptional cases</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Claim (1) - The exceptional cases\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>No pairing is possible for the exceptions listed above.\n</p><p><b>Proof.</b>\n</p>\n<dl><dd>case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598a16d4b7dde3dec3a390109882d54bb0308ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:\n<dl><dd>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> does not have a partner.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5218af40079081e694d8b82eeac2d368ef6ea76a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />:\n<dl><dd>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> does not have a partner.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e326b48726d4c73525c3b980409600fd87ea9846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />:\n<dl><dd>The only partner for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.</dd>\n<dd>With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> already occupied, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is left without a partner.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e3ccabf764b09e4f6297af9eb55a12fd4ae318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 10, 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />:\n<dl><dd>The only partner for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.</dd>\n<dd>With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> already occupied, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is left without a partner.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369bda3e2b33003ebf30b5739653915ced16dc1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 20, 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />:\n<dl><dd>The only partner for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.</dd>\n<dd>With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> already occupied, the only remaining partner for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.</dd>\n<dd>With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> already occupied, the only remaining partner for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.</dd>\n<dd>With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> already occupied, the only remaining partner for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.</dd>\n<dd>With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> already occupied, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is left without a partner.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<h3><span id=\"Claim_.282.29_-_Pairings_for_small_cases\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Claim_(2)_-_Pairings_for_small_cases\">Claim (2) - Pairings for small cases</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Claim (2) - Pairings for small cases\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Except for the exceptional cases, there is a pairing for each even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e67376d85a21889a01b76d7c9d8c765b2bac379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof.</b>\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb51701de990946766916139893b85112df58fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 8 : [[1, 8], [2, 7], [3, 6], [4, 5]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/40276bacc6fd97ad71ad4c3cd1cb6dc95b499aa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 14 : [[1, 8], [2, 14], [3, 13], [4, 12], [5, 11], [6, 10], [7, 9]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"425\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3eed3e3442676e2af129f4050a17024fb62c3f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 16 : [[1, 8], [2, 7], [3, 6], [4, 5], [9, 16], [10, 15], [11, 14], [12, 13]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"487\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/47129f960b610dc32874f4f5fa2992aa2bebca27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 18 : [[1, 15], [2, 14], [3, 13], [4, 12], [5, 11], [6, 10], [7, 18], [8, 17], [9, 16]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"550\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547005ccd207437571324ab2f90e2270aa39a4cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 24 : [[1, 24], [2, 23], [3, 22], [4, 21], [5, 20], [6, 19], [7, 18], [8, 17], [9, 16], [10, 15], [11, 14], [12, 13]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"738\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/8879cd96a7dd25befe1ac41db89b3592970373aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 26 : [[1, 15], [2, 14], [3, 22], [4, 21], [5, 20], [6, 19], [7, 18], [8, 17], [9, 16], [10, 26], [11, 25], [12, 24], [13, 23]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"800\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/9/93975572fa560ec45cfef1a8bbb8521512f2d380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 28 : [[1, 15], [2, 14], [3, 6], [4, 21], [5, 20], [7, 18], [8, 28], [9, 16], [10, 26], [11, 25], [12, 24], [13, 23], [17, 19], [22, 27]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"863\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9b9583bb9c33f28d4f49211f41150b49255e840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 30 : [[1, 3], [2, 14], [4, 5], [6, 30], [7, 18], [8, 28], [9, 16], [10, 26], [11, 25], [12, 24], [13, 23], [15, 21], [17, 19], [20, 29], [22, 27]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"926\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac24ca4459e173e9811a738966833e16cd6224b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 32 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 14], [12, 13], [15, 21], [17, 32], [18, 31], [19, 30], [20, 29], [22, 27], [23, 26], [24, 25]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"993\" height=\"20\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b2eff489b7ef14491320e974c34127436ea80fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 34 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 19], [8, 28], [9, 27], [10, 26], [11, 25], [12, 24], [13, 23], [14, 22], [15, 21], [16, 33], [17, 32], [18, 31], [20, 29], [30, 34]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1051\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6e485f11d333e211b76cb40ee5da197141d5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 36 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 21], [5, 20], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 27], [11, 25], [12, 24], [13, 36], [14, 22], [15, 34], [16, 33], [17, 32], [18, 31], [19, 30], [23, 26], [29, 35]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1113\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/5659c31d3e1df8ff0c0ab239ecc9e1388dabd548.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 38 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 21], [5, 20], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 27], [11, 38], [12, 37], [13, 36], [14, 22], [15, 34], [16, 33], [17, 32], [18, 31], [19, 30], [23, 26], [24, 25], [29, 35]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1176\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e030f20a417c71048c820ed2f2fd5658f6fc1ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 40 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 19], [8, 28], [9, 40], [10, 39], [11, 38], [12, 37], [13, 36], [14, 35], [15, 21], [16, 33], [17, 32], [18, 31], [20, 29], [22, 27], [23, 26], [24, 25], [30, 34]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1239\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/2138da211dc16164bdbdac9686d8ac247fe298f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 42 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 41], [9, 27], [11, 38], [12, 37], [13, 36], [14, 35], [15, 34], [16, 33], [17, 32], [18, 31], [19, 30], [20, 29], [21, 28], [22, 42], [23, 26], [24, 40], [25, 39]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1301\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/5373f7947edef8bf0631201532b5b3dcdb3788f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 44 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 27], [11, 14], [12, 37], [13, 36], [15, 34], [16, 33], [17, 32], [18, 31], [19, 30], [20, 44], [21, 43], [22, 42], [23, 41], [24, 40], [25, 39], [26, 38], [29, 35]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1364\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05a8b1e4b3a1775e4af7d6ee7d9131bb8079db3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 46 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 14], [12, 13], [15, 34], [17, 32], [18, 46], [19, 30], [20, 44], [21, 43], [22, 42], [23, 41], [24, 40], [25, 39], [26, 38], [27, 37], [29, 35], [31, 33], [36, 45]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1427\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/7/c77a06e9bf562dbbd813e06595cbe4a96ab97aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 48 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 14], [12, 13], [15, 21], [17, 32], [18, 31], [19, 30], [20, 29], [22, 27], [23, 26], [24, 25], [33, 48], [34, 47], [35, 46], [36, 45], [37, 44], [38, 43], [39, 42], [40, 41]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1489\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/0/6501280a105d1821cf3b53d6b73c72312e195a5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 50 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 14], [12, 13], [15, 34], [17, 47], [18, 46], [19, 30], [20, 44], [21, 43], [22, 42], [23, 41], [24, 40], [25, 39], [26, 38], [27, 37], [29, 35], [31, 50], [32, 49], [33, 48], [36, 45]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1552\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f24bb0dc76eee07575ca35fe3639ebbe259ac84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 52 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 14], [12, 52], [13, 36], [15, 34], [17, 47], [18, 46], [19, 45], [20, 44], [21, 43], [22, 42], [23, 41], [24, 40], [25, 39], [26, 38], [27, 37], [29, 35], [30, 51], [31, 50], [32, 49], [33, 48]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1614\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228909e038e19668e35fc2faf2fec7f9558b2a9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 54 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 53], [12, 37], [13, 36], [14, 35], [15, 34], [17, 47], [18, 46], [19, 45], [20, 44], [21, 43], [22, 42], [23, 41], [24, 40], [25, 39], [26, 38], [27, 54], [29, 52], [30, 51], [31, 50], [32, 49], [33, 48]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1677\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39e9ddb9ff408885807060f56d65fd446216ca79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 56 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 55], [11, 53], [12, 37], [13, 36], [14, 22], [15, 34], [16, 33], [17, 47], [18, 46], [19, 45], [20, 44], [21, 43], [23, 41], [24, 40], [25, 56], [26, 38], [27, 54], [29, 35], [30, 51], [31, 50], [32, 49], [39, 42], [48, 52]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1740\" height=\"18\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8a84fd6912198df142b3a8525a6e1e0b9170e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 58 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 55], [11, 53], [12, 37], [13, 36], [14, 22], [15, 34], [16, 33], [17, 47], [18, 46], [19, 45], [20, 44], [21, 43], [23, 58], [24, 57], [25, 56], [26, 38], [27, 54], [29, 35], [30, 51], [31, 50], [32, 49], [39, 42], [40, 41], [48, 52]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1807\" height=\"20\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d36aee71462c7f276e56119ac26bb3d5325e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 60 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 53], [12, 37], [13, 36], [14, 35], [15, 34], [17, 47], [18, 46], [19, 45], [20, 44], [21, 60], [22, 59], [23, 58], [24, 57], [25, 56], [26, 55], [27, 54], [29, 52], [30, 51], [31, 50], [32, 49], [33, 48], [38, 43], [39, 42], [40, 41]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1869\" height=\"20\" /></dd>\n<dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77eee7e9cd4d0e99b86b2339a880777b84fad9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 62 : [[1, 3], [2, 7], [4, 5], [6, 10], [8, 28], [9, 16], [11, 14], [12, 52], [13, 51], [15, 49], [17, 32], [18, 46], [19, 62], [20, 61], [21, 60], [22, 59], [23, 58], [24, 57], [25, 56], [26, 55], [27, 54], [29, 35], [30, 34], [31, 50], [33, 48], [36, 45], [37, 44], [38, 43], [39, 42], [40, 41], [47, 53]]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1928\" height=\"18\" /></dd></dl>\n<h3><span id=\"Claim_.283.29_-_The_main_inequality\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Claim_(3)_-_The_main_inequality\">Claim (3) - The main inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Claim (3) - The main inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192484d6b5ac0c65a3788df295fc5a8a46a6703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />, the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/419cffe6a11209547657ac1c278899bb92ee49f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68n \\leq n^2 + 276$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" /> holds.\n</p><p><b>Proof.</b> Proceed by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. The statement is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/aceb19ac350a8179aa719d524161ffa84bff9947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, since the lhs\nof the inequality evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/892ffa8a40ce219252f7cb80de3b53cfab59628a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4352$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> and the rhs evaluates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/b/a6b23c408f1c3804780906d0890faee467cef558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4372$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\nNow assume the statement is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192484d6b5ac0c65a3788df295fc5a8a46a6703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/6/406e87a45b368999907023b591f3dfaa3ca5f932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$68 \\leq 2n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />.\nAdding this inequality to the induction hypothesis gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21f3a58c829e77086d93c3bcedb9e86126960991.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[68n + 68 \\leq n^2 + 276 + 2n + 1\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>which simplifies to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/95365edf7ed9357dd45491b53a5b8c60e720bd42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[68(n + 1) \\leq (n + 1)^2 + 276\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>and this gives the statement for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Claim_.284.29_-_Rewriting_the_main_inequality\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Claim_(4)_-_Rewriting_the_main_inequality\">Claim (4) - Rewriting the main inequality</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Claim (4) - Rewriting the main inequality\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192484d6b5ac0c65a3788df295fc5a8a46a6703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />, the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c16b3f2c3e53ee125bf769ef40cff93f011871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 4\\sqrt{n + 25} + 29 \\leq 2n + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" /> holds.\n</p><p><b>Proof.</b> Start with the inequality from Claim (3).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55d1d75acbc3149349afe23183ab4f91a645858.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[68n \\leq n^2 + 276\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f3130f8445c3408c8a13cd100d70568f1a42d7eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52n$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> from both sides\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1cc54f4c3e5f5c3e50ca31e591b7459972baf7d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16n \\leq n^2 - 52n + 276\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8924412a12becf7905729885a46e3e351ec5a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> to both sides\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582ede04320b962795e4aa239cc973baa2788690.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16n + 400 \\leq n^2 - 52n + 676\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Factor both sides, using the binomial formula for the rhs\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/f/26fd01e3d4e602e4b55b9b9459a7d97a250d2de7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[16(n + 25) \\leq (n - 26)^2\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Take the square root of both sides\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/5066697b277b4e194a3c6a7b6cea8c3a9ab1699e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4\\sqrt{n + 25} \\leq n - 26\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Finally, adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/6/9e6842deb805bcaf8f281f5214e7aba8570ce0ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> to both sides gives the statement.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Claim_.285.29_-_Finding_odd_perfect_squares\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Claim_(5)_-_Finding_odd_perfect_squares\">Claim (5) - Finding odd perfect squares</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Claim (5) - Finding odd perfect squares\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For each even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192484d6b5ac0c65a3788df295fc5a8a46a6703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />, there is an odd perfect square in the closed interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45373aa6bafe6e2a39fd4827734c2df2ff7ec905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[n + 24, 2n - 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof.</b> Proceed by induction on the even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. The statement is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/aceb19ac350a8179aa719d524161ffa84bff9947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb660d29d6374931c3ccefdb683a819da9d8a39.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n + 24 = 88 \\leq 11^2 = 121 \\leq 127 = 2n - 1\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now assume that the statement is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, that is, there is\nan odd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/5/fd55734cac7c1c29035c31518e0d1d0f748e60ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 24 \\leq k^2 \\leq 2n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"167\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> is already\nat least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/a/82a22a3ccffb07627fcc75861f5497988c552d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> also satisfies the statement for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3be44477b1c4728ab06d90fde978271a2a909a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />,\nsince then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd884d84b7677000ca7e88303aedf7b572fabc84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n + 2) + 24 = n + 26 \\leq k^2 \\leq 2n - 1 \\leq 2n + 3 = 2(n + 2) - 1\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>The remaining case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71b5f2d01a74f4588c64d5bbc0f94d15de4a9252.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 24 \\leq k^2 &lt; n + 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"168\" height=\"17\" /> actually simplifies to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acb2c6c56cb5e9ccbf791c1d74d5c9adc418105c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2 = n + 25\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>since the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/614f06a4454425c00f5c25f4d50fb788c4459291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 = n + 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> is ruled out, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is odd.\nAdd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28f038a50595c2d43efef1ac831e39fb8de80f7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> to the equation above and obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/7/c1778755e0d4c9f23caf4536549503f4e5f27519.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2 + 4k + 4 = n + 4k + 29\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Factoring the lhs and replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in the rhs gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/f/bbfad55078ff0b2942c2b3b61b99dc6c551c2cca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(k + 2)^2 = n + 4\\sqrt{n + 25} + 29\\]\" width=\"234\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>By Claim (4), this expression is less or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d7541e1aba5382ac9300ffe7e659794d42b7c7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />.\nHence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/eba9a75444c45db8ebae8808f4b07fb9414d7a44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k + 2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" /> is an odd perfect square in the interval\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c21a11a93545b245b05b990bd8ba33ed86a083a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[(n + 2) + 24, 2(n + 2) - 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"18\" /> and this concludes the induction.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Finish\">The Finish</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: The Finish\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Using the claims, we prove the Main Statement by induction on the even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>By the Claims (1) and (2), the Main Statement is true for all even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b431b0122b542e2b814e28959aa74555f6b6106f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be even with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a192484d6b5ac0c65a3788df295fc5a8a46a6703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />.\nWith Claim (5), we find an odd perfect square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45373aa6bafe6e2a39fd4827734c2df2ff7ec905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[n + 24, 2n - 1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44c7dd125033696829589487a349dd5585aa08ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = k^2 - n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> and observe\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c8103250b3378761acb44c943d9d6fee7966eb06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24 \\leq p \\leq n - 1\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>which implies the stronger inequality\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f6d20379a2f844d2c0c1ce28803473b952723b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[24 &lt; p \\leq n - 1\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is odd. By construction of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />\nand hence are partners. Furthermore, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are of\nopposite parity, there is an even number of numbers strictly\nbetween them. These numbers may be paired up straightforward in the following way\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/6439485eba206792e0661dc4719c7d415cf106b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p + 1) + (n - 1) = k^2\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/13315bb6f1ed4d53fb96053acd304d9e58870b2e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p + 2) + (n - 2) = k^2\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/b/8fb1449a30e923666652d6f1a6bcf6574ad2f64a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p + 3) + (n - 3) = k^2\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/16762e47f22f53e2431935f211fa82570b46b6cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dots\\]\" width=\"18\" height=\"2\" />\n</p><p>Hence, in order to complete the pairing for all numbers up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />,\nit only remains to pair up the numbers up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7682fd18a877f0fc6b3eab0112f568c4fd1b732a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />.\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7682fd18a877f0fc6b3eab0112f568c4fd1b732a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> is even.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/8/8b8f56522958990d6a2f1cb1302388616dd15fbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64 \\leq p - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />, then apply Claim (5) recursively again, to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7682fd18a877f0fc6b3eab0112f568c4fd1b732a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> instead of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />,\nin order to pair up another portion of the yet unpaired numbers.\nEventually, we will reach a scenario where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5cae2f26cf3766ebe4becfc42c1368b8e24d2cc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1 \\leq 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />.\nBy the construction of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a6e1d3436f8c1dcb5b3af417d35ef33f748571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 \\leq p - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" />.\nHence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7682fd18a877f0fc6b3eab0112f568c4fd1b732a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> cannot be one of the exceptional cases and we may\napply Claim (2) to find a pairing for all the remaining numbers up to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7682fd18a877f0fc6b3eab0112f568c4fd1b732a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Credits\">Credits</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=KGS_math_club/solution_pairing&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Credits\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Work partially supported by suggestions and/or Thai food from/with Vladimir and Konrad.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018092512\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 739/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 29331/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:14897:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018092512 and revision id 77811. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}